From: hashtagbasit <53941105+hashtagbasit@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: qcom-hv-haptics: use the one-argument __assign_str()

The base config builds SM8550 without tracing, so the haptics trace event never
compiled. SteamOS needs CONFIG_FTRACE (tracefs for mangoapp and
steamos-manager), and since Linux 6.10 __assign_str() takes only the
destination; the source comes from the matching __string().
---
--- a/include/trace/events/qcom_haptics.h
+++ b/include/trace/events/qcom_haptics.h
@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@
 	),
 
 	TP_fast_assign(
-		__assign_str(id_name, name);
+		__assign_str(id_name);
 		__entry->msb = msb;
 		__entry->lsb = lsb;
 	),
